<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="60256" href="schedule/2014/fall/MATH/468/60256.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2014" href="schedule/2014.xml">2014</calendarYear><term id="120148" href="schedule/2014/fall.xml">Fall 2014</term><subject id="MATH" href="schedule/2014/fall/MATH.xml">Mathematics</subject><course id="468" href="schedule/2014/fall/MATH/468.xml">Topics in Applied Statistics</course></parents><sectionNumber>M1G</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Survival Analysis</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Introduction to the analysis of time-to-event outcomes. Topics include censoring, discrete survival, parametric models, nonparametric one- and K-sample methods, Cox regression, regression diagnostics, time-dependent covariates, and multivariate survival outcomes. Emphasis on key underlying concepts and practical implementation. Prerequisites: STAT 410 and knowledge of R. Recommended: STAT 420. Restricted to Statistics Graduate Students until May 5, 2014.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Closed</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2014-08-25Z</startDate><endDate>2014-12-10Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LEC">Lecture</type><start>11:00 AM</start><end>11:50 AM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MWF    </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>223</roomNumber><buildingName>Gregory Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Zhao" firstName="S">Zhao, S</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>